Seed 43 is in, but both length results from this arm are now void: the uncompressed baseline was cut off by the 32-token answer limit. Nothing is running. The campaign waits on your budget decision.

**Done this wake**
- **Seed-43 runs are healthy.** These are the compressed model on 20-page documents and on 40-passage text. Each has all 1,500 rows, every row judged, and the slot counts match the audit. The 20-page run was preempted 4 times and still completed.
- **The second judge prompt gives the same numbers** (one short GPU job, 2 min).

**What changed**
- **The answer limit cuts the uncompressed answers.** The shared eval script stops every answer at 32 tokens. That cuts the uncompressed model mid-sentence, and more often on longer inputs:

  | input | uncompressed answers cut by the limit |
  |---|---|
  | documents, 4 pages | 5.7% |
  | documents, 20 pages | 16.3% |
  | text, 10 passages | 32.9% |
  | text, 40 passages | 46.9% |

  The campaign's bar is under 5%. The compressed model is only cut on 0.6-5.9% of answers.
- **"At 20 pages the compressed model closes the gap" is withdrawn.**
  - Gap change from 4 to 20 pages, seeds 42 / 43: +4.3 / +3.1 points.
  - Same, on only the questions where no answer was cut: −0.6 / −2.0 points.
- **On text the picture flips toward a real loss.** On the uncut questions, the gap widens by 4.8 / 3.4 points from 10 to 40 passages. Those questions were chosen by looking at the answers, so this decides nothing.
- **Rule added:** a length result counts only if every file in the comparison has under 5% of answers cut. Re-runs use the 512-token limit, as the long-document runs already do. I also added a known-issues entry, and updated `docs/longdoc_diagnosis.md` with both seeds and the share of answers cut.
- **The long-document measurement is now the only clean length measurement.** It uses real documents of 4k-32k tokens or 10-40 pages, and already runs at the 512-token limit.

**Budget:** 32.0 of 60 GPU-hours used (counted from SLURM over all 57 jobs), and 57 of 70 jobs.

**Not saved:** a note about this answer-limit trap in the project memory. This run is not allowed to write there. Someone in a normal chat should add it.

Your decision (in `campaign_longdoc/BLOCKED.md`), on whether to measure on real long documents:

| option | GPU-hours | jobs | what you get |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1. full long-document measurement (recommended) | +54 (60 → 114) | +17 (70 → 87) | how the gap grows with length on real long documents, both seeds, text / pages / mixed; whether long-chunk training helps on long text |
| 2. option 1, plus the short-set length runs again at the 512-token limit (12 jobs) | +66 (→ 126) | +31 (→ 101) | also settles the 20-page and 40-passage questions on the usual eval sets |
| 3. option 1 without the long-chunk text runs | +39 (→ 99) | +13 (→ 83) | the length answer only |
| 4. stop | 0 | 0 | no length number decides anything |
